  "body": "## Summary\n\nLittle Say's iOS JavaScript export fails because Apple authentication imports `prop-types`, but the installed dependency graph does not provide it. Declare it as a mobile production dependency so clean locked installations can bundle the existing Apple authentication code.\n\nThe lockfile adds only `prop-types` 15.8.1 and its required nested `react-is` 16.13.1. Existing package versions, integrity hashes and classifications are unchanged; no provider code changes are needed.\n\nCloses #43.\n\n## Test plan and behavior evidence\n\n| Scenario | Expected and observed | Evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Install baseline and final source independently with `npm ci`, then resolve the import from AppleButton and export iOS. | Baseline fails with missing `prop-types`. Final resolves version 15.8.1 and its required APIs, then completes the full iOS JavaScript export. Neither installation uses copied or junctioned dependencies. | [Before/After output and reproduction](https://github.com/MChartier/little-say/blob/59a85fcf200da63e3a470c8e7847bab347a67161/README.md#before-and-after-observable-contract) |\n| Export Android/web and run repository checks from the fresh final installation. | Both exports pass, along with 288 tests, type checks, server build and release metadata validation. | [Native exports](https://github.com/MChartier/little-say/blob/59a85fcf200da63e3a470c8e7847bab347a67161/issue43-native-exports.log) · [Repository checks](https://github.com/MChartier/little-say/blob/59a85fcf200da63e3a470c8e7847bab347a67161/issue43-check.log) |\n\nThis is non-UI dependency resolution; real CLI output is the observable Before/After contract. [Provenance](https://github.com/MChartier/little-say/blob/59a85fcf200da63e3a470c8e7847bab347a67161/provenance.json) binds actual master `fabb925c`, final source `a570b52c`, independent installations, commands and bundle hashes.\n\n## Limitations\n\nJavaScript export success does not establish a signed iOS build, TestFlight readiness, device behavior or real Apple sign-in. Those checks were not performed. No credentials, provider setup, cloud build, release or deployment is included.\n\nImplementing task: `01a11ca6-7faa-7628-8031-ac89bc018019`. Independent review and CI results are recorded in the PR discussion.\n",
